    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Begley are proud to introduce Killinure, Glasson to te market.\n\nNestled in a peaceful countryside setting, this detached bungalow presents a fantastic opportunity for those looking to create a truly special home. Having been unoccupied for a number of years, the property offers exceptional potential for renovation and modernisation, making it an ideal purchase for homeowners, investors or anyone dreaming of a tranquil rural retreat.\n\nOccupying a generous site, the accommodation comprises an entrance hall, kitchen, spacious living room, three well-proportioned bedrooms, a wet room and an attached garage, offering excellent storage or exciting potential for conversion into additional living space (subject to the necessary planning permission).\n\nAdding to its appeal, the property may qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, allowing eligible purchasers to benefit from Government funding to restore and transform the home (subject to the terms and conditions of the scheme).\n\nThe location is one of the property's standout features. Just 1.6km from the scenic Portlick Forest, with its beautiful woodland walks and lakeside trails and only 3.9km from the award-winning village of Glasson, affectionately known as the \"Village of the Roses\", you'll enjoy the very best of country living. The shores of Lough Ree are also within easy reach, offering endless opportunities for boating, fishing, kayaking and waterside recreation. Athlone is just a 20-minute drive away, providing an excellent range of shopping, dining, schools and transport links, while Ballymahon and the renowned Centre Parcs Longford Forest are approximately 15km away.\n\nWhether you're searching for a forever family home, a charming holiday escape or an exciting renovation project with significant potential to add value, this property offers a rare opportunity to create something truly exceptional in one of the region's most sought-after countryside locations."
      },
